WEBVTT

﻿1

00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:26.566
Once more, my friend.


00:01:26.599 --> 00:01:28.235
Once more.


00:02:21.821 --> 00:02:23.290
Yah!


00:02:26.326 --> 00:02:27.794
Yah! Yah!


00:13:59.118 --> 00:14:02.353
Let him go.


00:14:02.354 --> 00:14:04.222
I have to take you home.


00:14:04.223 --> 00:14:07.358
Let me go.


00:14:07.359 --> 00:14:11.062
I don't want to go back.


00:14:11.063 --> 00:14:15.366
You can rest in peace there,
with your father and his father.


00:14:15.367 --> 00:14:18.970
Look at him.
He is far by now.


00:14:18.971 --> 00:14:21.906
I want to go home.


00:14:21.907 --> 00:14:23.409
I know.


00:14:25.878 --> 00:14:28.047
Now he's free.


00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:34.052
Why do you smile?


00:14:34.053 --> 00:14:37.455
He's at peace now.


00:14:37.456 --> 00:14:40.058
Let him go then.


00:14:40.059 --> 00:14:43.761
I'll not leave you alone.
I gave you my pledge.


00:14:43.762 --> 00:14:46.898
And I will honour that pledge.


00:14:46.899 --> 00:14:49.233
I'll bring you back to
your mother and your sisters.


00:14:49.234 --> 00:14:51.903
I'm not alone.


00:14:51.904 --> 00:14:54.573
No.


00:14:57.643 --> 00:15:00.279
No.


00:18:53.378 --> 00:18:56.549
Return to your path, stranger.


00:18:57.649 --> 00:19:01.052
Why do you do this?


00:19:01.053 --> 00:19:04.822
He must pay for that
which he has done.


00:19:04.823 --> 00:19:06.657
What is his crime?


00:19:06.658 --> 00:19:07.658
He is a thief.


00:19:07.659 --> 00:19:09.562
It's not true, sire.


00:19:12.564 --> 00:19:16.367
Help me, please.
I beg of you!


00:19:16.368 --> 00:19:18.002
Silence!


00:19:18.003 --> 00:19:19.070
What was stolen?


00:19:19.071 --> 00:19:20.504
Our rabbits.


00:19:20.505 --> 00:19:24.408
Lies! Nothing but lies!


00:19:24.409 --> 00:19:26.844
You would kill him
for stealing rabbits?


00:19:26.845 --> 00:19:28.581
This is not your business,
stranger.


00:19:33.018 --> 00:19:34.685
This is my path.


00:19:34.686 --> 00:19:36.923
Our lives are now one.


00:19:38.857 --> 00:19:41.926
You're brave, soldier,


00:19:41.927 --> 00:19:44.795
brave but stupid.


00:19:44.796 --> 00:19:47.531
You can hardly stand.


00:19:47.532 --> 00:19:50.570
And yet you think
you can give me orders?


00:19:52.304 --> 00:19:54.705
Go.


00:19:54.706 --> 00:19:57.777
I won't tell you again.


00:20:01.913 --> 00:20:04.817
Kill him.


00:21:35.974 --> 00:21:37.908
No, please.


00:21:37.909 --> 00:21:40.010
I'll not harm you.


00:21:40.011 --> 00:21:42.546
Who are you?


00:21:42.547 --> 00:21:45.316
I've not seen you
around here before.


00:21:45.317 --> 00:21:48.220
I've not been
around here before.


00:21:50.989 --> 00:21:55.192
Then it was fate
that brought you here.


00:21:55.193 --> 00:21:59.063
They would have killed me.


00:21:59.064 --> 00:22:02.833
I thank you.
You saved my life.


00:22:02.834 --> 00:22:06.537
By taking more life.


00:22:06.538 --> 00:22:10.674
They left you no choice.


00:22:10.675 --> 00:22:14.011
Perhaps, but I've not always
made the right choice.


00:22:14.012 --> 00:22:17.348
Nor have I.


00:22:17.349 --> 00:22:21.519
But now, I am just an old man,


00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:23.954
and it is life that chooses.


00:22:23.955 --> 00:22:26.757
You are wrong.


00:22:26.758 --> 00:22:29.195
Are you sure, stranger?


00:22:55.387 --> 00:22:57.988
Who is he?


00:22:57.989 --> 00:23:02.293
An old friend.


00:23:02.294 --> 00:23:06.664
What happened to him?


00:23:06.665 --> 00:23:10.301
We are soldiers.


00:23:10.302 --> 00:23:15.005
I understand.


00:23:15.006 --> 00:23:16.440
Are you hungry?


00:23:16.441 --> 00:23:19.978
Yes. I have nothing.


00:23:25.750 --> 00:23:27.719
That's what you think.


00:23:43.969 --> 00:23:46.670
Where are you from?


00:23:46.671 --> 00:23:49.673
The battlefields in the south.


00:23:49.674 --> 00:23:52.977
"The battlefields"?


00:23:52.978 --> 00:23:56.282
And who won, if I may ask?


00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:00.551
Nobody, I believe.


00:24:00.552 --> 00:24:04.223
"Nobody"?
What do you mean, "Nobody"?


00:24:06.458 --> 00:24:10.628
Somebody must have won.
Somebody always wins.


00:24:10.629 --> 00:24:14.131
Not this time.


00:24:14.132 --> 00:24:17.535
I understand.


00:24:17.536 --> 00:24:21.805
Strange thing, war.


00:24:21.806 --> 00:24:26.210
I fought once.


00:24:26.211 --> 00:24:29.547
Many years ago.


00:24:29.548 --> 00:24:34.218
But in those times,
somebody always won.


00:24:34.219 --> 00:24:36.987
Times have changed.


00:24:36.988 --> 00:24:39.156
Times have changed.


00:24:39.157 --> 00:24:41.692
I don't like it.


00:24:41.693 --> 00:24:43.527
What?


00:24:43.528 --> 00:24:45.829
The war.


00:24:45.830 --> 00:24:48.666
Why?


00:24:48.667 --> 00:24:51.101
Because you die in war.


00:24:51.102 --> 00:24:54.371
Ask your friend here.


00:24:54.372 --> 00:24:56.942
War means death.


00:25:21.366 --> 00:25:23.434
So, you told me
where you're from.


00:25:23.435 --> 00:25:25.703
But you haven't told me
where you're going.


00:25:25.704 --> 00:25:30.407
You ask a lot of questions,
old man.


00:25:30.408 --> 00:25:33.377
Well, where are you going?


00:25:33.378 --> 00:25:36.046
East.


00:25:36.047 --> 00:25:38.048
"East".


00:25:38.049 --> 00:25:42.588
And is there anyone
waiting for you?


00:25:44.656 --> 00:25:47.391
No.


00:25:47.392 --> 00:25:50.394
"No"?


00:25:50.395 --> 00:25:52.930
So, why do you travel?


00:25:52.931 --> 00:25:55.834
For him.


00:26:07.078 --> 00:26:10.581
"For him"?


00:26:10.582 --> 00:26:13.917
Don't tell me he's got somebody
waiting for him.


00:26:13.918 --> 00:26:17.489
Watch what you say, old man.


00:26:19.858 --> 00:26:22.660
Forgive my tongue, soldier.


00:26:22.661 --> 00:26:27.166
Sometimes, I can't control it.


00:26:31.503 --> 00:26:34.006
His blood still stains my hands.


00:26:35.840 --> 00:26:40.646
I will bury him,
in the land of our fathers.


00:26:45.116 --> 00:26:46.784
He must sleep...


00:26:46.785 --> 00:26:49.888
in peace.


00:26:59.464 --> 00:27:02.001
Sleep well, soldier.


00:27:03.068 --> 00:27:06.171
Sleep well.


00:31:33.171 --> 00:31:34.506
Stop!


00:31:39.610 --> 00:31:42.213
Stop, I say.


00:31:44.749 --> 00:31:46.485
And for what reason, stranger?


00:31:49.253 --> 00:31:51.790
That body you carry with you
does not belong to you.


00:31:53.124 --> 00:31:56.593
I don't understand
what you mean.


00:31:56.594 --> 00:31:59.596
The body, it's mine.


00:31:59.597 --> 00:32:03.433
Yours?


00:32:03.434 --> 00:32:08.305
I don't think so, stranger.
It's mine, always has been.


00:32:08.306 --> 00:32:10.440
You are mistaken, old woman.


00:32:10.441 --> 00:32:13.610
"Mistaken"?


00:32:13.611 --> 00:32:16.513
Are you telling me
I wouldn't recognize


00:32:16.514 --> 00:32:19.017
the body of my own son?


00:32:22.620 --> 00:32:25.288
He's not your son.


00:32:25.289 --> 00:32:28.625
Mind what you say.


00:32:28.626 --> 00:32:30.529
I know what I say.


00:32:32.964 --> 00:32:35.632
And it's you who should beware.


00:32:35.633 --> 00:32:40.170
I know his mother. You have
nothing to do with him.


00:32:40.171 --> 00:32:43.308
I know him.


00:32:48.212 --> 00:32:51.181
And I know you.


00:32:51.182 --> 00:32:53.550
What?


00:32:53.551 --> 00:32:55.852
I know you, soldier.


00:32:55.853 --> 00:32:59.656
I have known you
for a long, long time.


00:32:59.657 --> 00:33:03.562
Your star will not
shine forever.


00:33:04.662 --> 00:33:06.696
And your path is long.


00:33:06.697 --> 00:33:09.699
You are a witch.


00:33:09.700 --> 00:33:12.836
You accuse me?


00:33:12.837 --> 00:33:15.672
I accuse you, witch.


00:33:15.673 --> 00:33:18.076
Return what you have stolen.
And I will spare you.


00:33:24.282 --> 00:33:29.220
You would deprive a mother
of her only son?


00:33:31.222 --> 00:33:33.890
Oh. You're angry, soldier.


00:33:33.891 --> 00:33:37.794
I am tired.


00:33:37.795 --> 00:33:40.263
You should rest then.


00:33:40.264 --> 00:33:43.233
I will rest when I
have returned him home.


00:33:43.234 --> 00:33:46.203
Stubborn.


00:33:46.204 --> 00:33:49.775
You have no idea.


00:33:50.875 --> 00:33:54.444
So, it was you.


00:33:54.445 --> 00:33:58.715
In the woods.
You followed me.


00:33:58.716 --> 00:34:01.718
Yeah.


00:34:01.719 --> 00:34:04.454
Enough. Return to your path
if you wish to live.


00:34:04.455 --> 00:34:07.958
And if I were to tell you that
our paths were the same?


00:34:07.959 --> 00:34:11.561
There is no place for you
on my path.


00:34:11.562 --> 00:34:14.297
There's no place for anybody.


00:34:14.298 --> 00:34:18.468
You win, soldier.


00:34:18.469 --> 00:34:21.406
My son will go with you.


00:34:29.113 --> 00:34:31.748
But beware.


00:34:31.749 --> 00:34:35.952
There is nothing worse
than the rage of a mother.


00:34:35.953 --> 00:34:37.621
You are not his mother!


00:34:37.622 --> 00:34:40.323
Yes, I am!


00:34:40.324 --> 00:34:44.928
Yes, I am mother
of all those like you.


00:34:44.929 --> 00:34:47.165
You are all mine.


00:34:58.376 --> 00:35:01.313
I will not forget you.


00:35:03.614 --> 00:35:07.686
I will not forget.


00:35:08.786 --> 00:35:10.922
Nor will I.


00:37:29.527 --> 00:37:34.465
For days, I wanted to ask you
where are we headed?


00:37:37.768 --> 00:37:41.139
You always ask
such stupid questions.


00:37:43.808 --> 00:37:47.711
I am tired.


00:37:47.712 --> 00:37:50.649
And what a joke today.


00:37:53.117 --> 00:37:55.618
This time, you are mistaken,
my friend.


00:37:55.619 --> 00:38:00.523
I was not asking
a stupid question.


00:38:00.524 --> 00:38:04.029
Why don't you remember
why we left in the first place?


00:38:09.967 --> 00:38:13.970
I am so hungry.


00:38:13.971 --> 00:38:17.375
I will hunt tomorrow.


00:38:22.313 --> 00:38:25.515
You remember?


00:38:25.516 --> 00:38:28.420
When we were young?


00:38:32.089 --> 00:38:34.492
You always got the bigger deer.


00:38:35.559 --> 00:38:39.562
Yes. This I remember.


00:38:39.563 --> 00:38:41.566
Much time has passed.


00:38:44.435 --> 00:38:46.571
Two wars...


00:38:53.944 --> 00:38:58.214
That last battle was a massacre.


00:38:58.215 --> 00:39:03.019
"Massacre" you said?


00:39:03.020 --> 00:39:06.856
Well, we fight till we die.


00:39:06.857 --> 00:39:11.194
That's all we know.


00:39:11.195 --> 00:39:14.864
Now I think the victory
would be to return home,


00:39:14.865 --> 00:39:19.469
grow old in peace.


00:39:19.470 --> 00:39:24.474
"Peace"?


00:39:24.475 --> 00:39:26.576
I don't think that men like us


00:39:26.577 --> 00:39:30.246
will ever be able to understand
the meaning of peace.


00:39:30.247 --> 00:39:34.584
What I remember was...


00:39:34.585 --> 00:39:36.719
smell, blood,


00:39:36.720 --> 00:39:41.559
mud, muck.


00:39:42.626 --> 00:39:45.563
You will have peace soon.


00:39:49.233 --> 00:39:51.770
Morning Star will guide us.


00:39:56.907 --> 00:40:00.478
We're heading east.


00:40:01.846 --> 00:40:04.982
Look at me.


00:42:40.738 --> 00:42:42.939
Take off the hood.


00:42:42.940 --> 00:42:46.811
We need to make sure
she's alive for the trial.


00:42:49.647 --> 00:42:52.915
Well?
What are you waiting for?


00:42:52.916 --> 00:42:54.784
I'm not going to do it.


00:42:54.785 --> 00:42:56.821
Just make sure you don't
look her in the eyes.


00:43:05.963 --> 00:43:10.635
Secure the area.


00:43:54.011 --> 00:43:56.713
Release the woman, and there'll
be no further bloodshed.


00:43:56.714 --> 00:44:01.517
That creature you call a "woman"
is already dead.


00:44:01.518 --> 00:44:03.486
You're wasting your time,


00:44:03.487 --> 00:44:06.222
and losing your dignity.


00:44:06.223 --> 00:44:08.891
And now you will lose something
more precious to you:


00:44:08.892 --> 00:44:10.660
your life.


00:44:10.661 --> 00:44:14.330
A soldier who is willing to kill
defending a witch


00:44:14.331 --> 00:44:16.999
deserves nothing less.


00:44:17.000 --> 00:44:19.502
Unless of course, there is
something human left within you.


00:44:19.503 --> 00:44:23.740
I do not practice witchcraft.


00:44:23.741 --> 00:44:26.275
And if she does,
I know the course of action.


00:44:26.276 --> 00:44:29.779
That woman saved my life.
And I would speak with her.


00:44:29.780 --> 00:44:32.983
Men of arms like yourself
should understand.


00:44:34.685 --> 00:44:37.353
You have just killed
one of my best men.


00:44:37.354 --> 00:44:41.090
And you try to convince me to
release a demon worshipper?


00:44:41.091 --> 00:44:43.693
What race of man are you?


00:44:43.694 --> 00:44:45.895
You speak like a leader.


00:44:45.896 --> 00:44:48.564
But you are nothing,
nothing but a worthless puppet


00:44:48.565 --> 00:44:52.235
in the hands of a witch.


00:44:52.236 --> 00:44:55.705
Your man attacked me.


00:44:55.706 --> 00:44:57.707
We fought fairly and
he died a soldier's death.


00:44:57.708 --> 00:45:00.643
You should honour his defeat


00:45:00.644 --> 00:45:03.748
instead of bleating
like a lost sheep.


00:45:09.386 --> 00:45:13.389
Now release her
and no one else need die.


00:45:13.390 --> 00:45:15.057
I've met men like you,


00:45:15.058 --> 00:45:18.427
veterans of duels
fought without honour.


00:45:18.428 --> 00:45:22.098
Men willing to judge without
being judged themselves,


00:45:22.099 --> 00:45:24.834
stained with the most
heinous of crimes,


00:45:24.835 --> 00:45:27.103
yet on the battlefield
you hide in the mud


00:45:27.104 --> 00:45:29.806
to save your own lives.


00:45:29.807 --> 00:45:31.974
I have killed many worms
like you,


00:45:31.975 --> 00:45:33.811
and today I shall kill another.


00:45:36.079 --> 00:45:38.447
Answer me this:


00:45:38.448 --> 00:45:41.586
where did you meet
this... woman?


00:45:43.353 --> 00:45:45.189
On the battlefield?


00:45:47.491 --> 00:45:50.092
I see I'm right.


00:45:50.093 --> 00:45:51.627
You fool.


00:45:51.628 --> 00:45:53.329
Have you never
seen women like this,


00:45:53.330 --> 00:45:55.631
scavenging amongst
the corpses like...


00:45:55.632 --> 00:45:58.968
like wolves
attracted to the kill?


00:45:58.969 --> 00:46:00.636
You are defending a witch


00:46:00.637 --> 00:46:02.473
because your mind
is already hers.


00:46:04.174 --> 00:46:06.177
But I pity you.


00:46:07.644 --> 00:46:09.345
Put down your sword


00:46:09.346 --> 00:46:11.015
and I will be willing
to save your life.


00:46:13.984 --> 00:46:16.118
Where I am headed,
there are priests


00:46:16.119 --> 00:46:19.322
who will be able to judge your
situation better than I can.


00:46:19.323 --> 00:46:21.490
I'm not offering you a truce,


00:46:21.491 --> 00:46:25.462
I'm offering you
the chance to save your soul.


00:46:28.398 --> 00:46:30.401
Agh!


00:46:44.514 --> 00:46:46.116
Agh!


00:47:06.236 --> 00:47:08.172
You stay right there.


00:47:10.540 --> 00:47:12.909
You risk your life to save me
and now you want to kill me.


00:47:12.910 --> 00:47:15.444
I don't want to kill you.


00:47:15.445 --> 00:47:18.447
I want to know who you are.


00:47:18.448 --> 00:47:21.050
What you are.


00:47:21.051 --> 00:47:24.854
The first time we met,
you were dying.


00:47:24.855 --> 00:47:27.857
I saved your life


00:47:27.858 --> 00:47:30.126
just as you have saved mine.
I believe at this point,


00:47:30.127 --> 00:47:32.061
the best thing to do is
to trust each other.


00:47:32.062 --> 00:47:35.366
I will lower my sword
when you answer me.


00:47:37.234 --> 00:47:40.102
I mean it.


00:47:40.103 --> 00:47:43.239
You showed me
one corpse amongst many men.


00:47:43.240 --> 00:47:46.811
How did you know
I was looking for him?


00:47:49.379 --> 00:47:51.414
You too think I am a witch.


00:47:51.415 --> 00:47:55.251
I think...


00:47:55.252 --> 00:47:58.754
I think I have taken
some trouble for you here,


00:47:58.755 --> 00:48:03.059
and there is a blade at
your throat, so I should answer.


00:48:03.060 --> 00:48:05.461
I will give you all the answers
you are looking for


00:48:05.462 --> 00:48:08.799
but right now
you will listen to me.


00:48:18.842 --> 00:48:20.377
No.


00:49:14.331 --> 00:49:16.198
You will heal soon.


00:49:16.199 --> 00:49:18.300
The wound is not deep.


00:49:18.301 --> 00:49:20.604
You were lucky, soldier.


00:49:25.342 --> 00:49:28.179
Where are we?


00:49:30.147 --> 00:49:32.750
In a safe place.


00:49:34.651 --> 00:49:36.554
No one can find you here.


00:49:40.357 --> 00:49:42.259
How did I get here?


00:49:46.863 --> 00:49:48.831
I saw a man with you.


00:49:48.832 --> 00:49:50.166
Shh.


00:49:50.167 --> 00:49:53.836
You're here and you are safe.


00:49:53.837 --> 00:49:56.707
That's all that matters now.


00:49:59.042 --> 00:50:00.910
I have a body with me.


00:50:00.911 --> 00:50:02.980
I have to get it.
I have to take him home.


00:50:04.214 --> 00:50:06.715
You must lie down.


00:50:06.716 --> 00:50:09.219
I haven't finished yet.


00:50:11.888 --> 00:50:13.791
Won't take long.


00:50:17.427 --> 00:50:19.563
What are you doing to me?


00:50:23.233 --> 00:50:26.902
You men of arms
place your trust in no one.


00:50:26.903 --> 00:50:30.873
This makes you blind.


00:50:30.874 --> 00:50:32.908
You are unable to distinguish
between who wants to help you


00:50:32.909 --> 00:50:34.979
and who wants to harm you.


00:50:37.080 --> 00:50:39.248
Maybe,


00:50:39.249 --> 00:50:41.750
but I understand enough


00:50:41.751 --> 00:50:44.453
to know that a woman
who lives in the woods


00:50:44.454 --> 00:50:46.590
cannot have studied healing.


00:50:48.658 --> 00:50:52.061
You're right.


00:50:52.062 --> 00:50:54.430
But there are many sources
of knowledge.


00:50:54.431 --> 00:50:58.335
Living in the woods
teaches you many things.


00:51:03.940 --> 00:51:06.142
There is no greater school
than that


00:51:06.143 --> 00:51:10.114
which is born from the pure
instinct of survival.


00:51:17.487 --> 00:51:20.324
You live here alone?


00:51:22.425 --> 00:51:25.362
I fled my lands
when the witch-hunting began.


00:51:27.964 --> 00:51:30.833
I've never returned.


00:51:30.834 --> 00:51:32.770
Why is that?


00:51:35.205 --> 00:51:37.041
I was afraid.


00:51:42.712 --> 00:51:45.382
I saw my sisters
burn in front of me.


00:51:48.018 --> 00:51:51.956
They tortured my mother
and left her to drown.


00:51:54.191 --> 00:51:56.158
There was no other choice.


00:51:56.159 --> 00:51:57.860
If I had stayed...


00:51:57.861 --> 00:52:02.233
I would have suffered
the same fate.


00:52:07.003 --> 00:52:11.173
They have never stopped
looking for me.


00:52:11.174 --> 00:52:13.309
I took a risk by venturing
onto that battlefield


00:52:13.310 --> 00:52:15.279
and they found me.


00:52:16.846 --> 00:52:18.749
But I found you.


00:52:31.194 --> 00:52:35.364
How did you know that man
was important to me?


00:52:35.365 --> 00:52:38.102
My mother taught us many things.


00:52:43.873 --> 00:52:46.944
We would sit in the woods
for days by the fire.


00:52:49.379 --> 00:52:53.884
My sisters and I had to learn
to sit and listen.


00:52:56.186 --> 00:52:59.256
My mother called it
The Voice of the Night.


00:53:02.392 --> 00:53:04.893
Once you had learned
to hear its presence,


00:53:04.894 --> 00:53:07.197
it would never leave you.


00:53:16.139 --> 00:53:20.376
Why do you still not answer me?


00:53:20.377 --> 00:53:22.911
You're wrong.


00:53:22.912 --> 00:53:27.116
I've already given you all
the answers you're looking for.


00:53:27.117 --> 00:53:30.252
Now tell me of you.


00:53:30.253 --> 00:53:33.255
After all,
you owe me that at least.


00:53:33.256 --> 00:53:35.491
This is already
the second favour


00:53:35.492 --> 00:53:37.261
I have granted you, soldier.


00:53:44.301 --> 00:53:46.937
I too left my home.


00:53:49.673 --> 00:53:52.176
Many years ago.


00:53:54.277 --> 00:53:58.781
The last 10 years of my life,


00:53:58.782 --> 00:54:02.686
I have been fighting
other men's wars.


00:54:06.122 --> 00:54:09.026
I have few happy tales to tell.


00:54:10.960 --> 00:54:14.296
You see?


00:54:14.297 --> 00:54:18.767
We have something in common.


00:54:18.768 --> 00:54:22.806
We both know what it's like
to leave our homes.


00:54:26.142 --> 00:54:29.046
I have never felt homesick.


00:54:31.614 --> 00:54:34.518
I lost my parents
when I was a child.


00:54:37.287 --> 00:54:40.222
The battlefield became my home.


00:54:40.223 --> 00:54:42.391
So why do you suffer so much?


00:54:42.392 --> 00:54:46.995
Your eyes do not lie.


00:54:46.996 --> 00:54:49.732
Even a warrior must have
someone waiting for them.


00:54:49.733 --> 00:54:53.635
Friends...


00:54:53.636 --> 00:54:55.539
a woman.


00:54:57.040 --> 00:55:01.844
The body I carry with me,


00:55:01.845 --> 00:55:05.749
he was the best friend
I ever had.


00:55:07.350 --> 00:55:10.018
I know.


00:55:10.019 --> 00:55:13.156
And who is she?


00:55:18.194 --> 00:55:20.864
He took her away from me.


00:56:40.410 --> 00:56:42.911
You see?


00:56:42.912 --> 00:56:45.816
I told you you would heal soon.


00:56:52.689 --> 00:56:54.625
Impossible.


00:56:56.926 --> 00:56:58.829
What have you done to me?


00:57:01.931 --> 00:57:03.765
That soldier was right!


00:57:03.766 --> 00:57:06.370
You should rest.


00:57:15.645 --> 00:57:19.749
You're not afraid of me,
are you, soldier?


00:57:22.018 --> 00:57:23.920
I must go.


01:02:50.346 --> 01:02:52.981
No! Wait!


01:02:52.982 --> 01:02:54.518
Wait!


01:05:58.334 --> 01:06:01.136
You have no respect, stranger.


01:06:01.137 --> 01:06:04.005
You enter my home
with your weapon drawn.


01:06:04.006 --> 01:06:07.175
Forgive me, my liege.


01:06:07.176 --> 01:06:11.079
Somebody was watching me.


01:06:11.080 --> 01:06:15.016
I came into your castle.


01:06:15.017 --> 01:06:17.519
Somebody?


01:06:17.520 --> 01:06:22.090
There is no "somebody" here.


01:06:22.091 --> 01:06:26.861
Only you and I...


01:06:26.862 --> 01:06:30.999
and my guards.


01:06:31.000 --> 01:06:33.701
You perhaps...


01:06:33.702 --> 01:06:36.104
are lost.


01:06:36.105 --> 01:06:38.506
I have a long way to travel.


01:06:38.507 --> 01:06:42.045
Then rest here.


01:06:44.113 --> 01:06:48.585
We have not had visitors
for many years.


01:06:51.087 --> 01:06:54.856
They used to travel from afar...


01:06:54.857 --> 01:06:58.561
to enjoy my hospitality.


01:07:02.298 --> 01:07:05.400
Times, my friend,


01:07:05.401 --> 01:07:07.602
have changed.


01:07:07.603 --> 01:07:11.139
Who would dare stay here?


01:07:11.140 --> 01:07:14.877
Be careful what you say.


01:07:16.545 --> 01:07:18.880
You may not see,


01:07:18.881 --> 01:07:22.750
but this place seems
the Devil's own.


01:07:22.751 --> 01:07:26.988
Leave the Devil in peace.


01:07:26.989 --> 01:07:29.991
He has no part


01:07:29.992 --> 01:07:33.761
In this story,


01:07:33.762 --> 01:07:38.401
man chooses his own destiny.


01:07:42.171 --> 01:07:45.940
His choices makes his future.


01:07:45.941 --> 01:07:48.243
The Lord...


01:07:48.244 --> 01:07:51.579
or the Devil...


01:07:51.580 --> 01:07:55.018
do not have the power
to change man's will.


01:07:57.186 --> 01:07:59.587
That is blasphemy.


01:07:59.588 --> 01:08:01.990
No.


01:08:01.991 --> 01:08:04.959
It is free will.


01:08:04.960 --> 01:08:09.297
Do not hide behind the Lord
for the choices you make.


01:08:09.298 --> 01:08:12.869
Do not take
the Lord's name in vain.


01:08:14.770 --> 01:08:19.507
I have never asked forgiveness
for the choices I have made.


01:08:19.508 --> 01:08:22.443
The Lord...


01:08:22.444 --> 01:08:25.780
or the Devil...


01:08:25.781 --> 01:08:30.520
should not concern themselves
over the path I have chosen.


01:08:34.223 --> 01:08:37.193
I am a king.


01:08:38.827 --> 01:08:41.162
And if I remember well,


01:08:41.163 --> 01:08:44.232
that should mean something.


01:08:44.233 --> 01:08:48.203
If the paths you have taken
have brought you to this,


01:08:48.204 --> 01:08:50.672
perhaps you should ask
for forgiveness


01:08:50.673 --> 01:08:52.340
before it is too late.


01:08:52.341 --> 01:08:55.843
Late for what, stranger?


01:08:55.844 --> 01:08:58.980
I have had my whole life...


01:08:58.981 --> 01:09:01.818
to ask for forgiveness.


01:09:04.019 --> 01:09:07.689
And I didn't.


01:09:07.690 --> 01:09:12.060
I chose all this.


01:09:12.061 --> 01:09:13.997
Why?


01:09:16.198 --> 01:09:18.733
Why?


01:09:18.734 --> 01:09:22.605
Why I prefer power to servitude?


01:09:23.906 --> 01:09:27.944
Why I chose riches to poverty?


01:09:31.180 --> 01:09:35.218
These are the questions
of a fool!


01:09:36.885 --> 01:09:38.519
I have heard enough.


01:09:38.520 --> 01:09:41.389
It is time for me to leave.


01:09:41.390 --> 01:09:45.260
You will never leave this place!


01:09:45.261 --> 01:09:48.263
You will stay...


01:09:48.264 --> 01:09:50.366
or you will die.


01:09:53.569 --> 01:09:56.205
It is your choice.


01:09:58.374 --> 01:10:00.708
I am leaving.


01:10:00.709 --> 01:10:02.410
Well...


01:10:02.411 --> 01:10:04.314
Then you must choose.


01:10:08.050 --> 01:10:10.954
Roll the dice.


01:12:02.197 --> 01:12:06.936
You see how easy it is
to choose?


01:12:42.104 --> 01:12:44.574
We have stopped again.


01:12:51.547 --> 01:12:53.449
I had to rest.


01:12:56.084 --> 01:12:59.220
I know. I'm sorry.


01:12:59.221 --> 01:13:01.589
It is my fault.


01:13:01.590 --> 01:13:03.257
No.


01:13:03.258 --> 01:13:05.161
It's my bones.


01:13:08.263 --> 01:13:12.099
They feel the winters more
these days.


01:13:12.100 --> 01:13:14.937
We still have a long way to go.


01:13:17.473 --> 01:13:20.410
We are lost.
Is that not the case?


01:13:34.523 --> 01:13:38.094
I took a wrong turn.


01:13:40.529 --> 01:13:42.465
So tell me, what now?


01:13:46.835 --> 01:13:50.338
Don't worry, my friend.


01:13:50.339 --> 01:13:53.641
It's not the first time
we've been lost.


01:13:53.642 --> 01:13:56.110
I still hope.


01:13:56.111 --> 01:13:58.980
Strange.


01:13:58.981 --> 01:14:02.049
Hope is the last thing
I remember.


01:14:02.050 --> 01:14:05.152
That was the moment
on the battlefield


01:14:05.153 --> 01:14:07.855
where I thought,
I would make it.


01:14:07.856 --> 01:14:11.526
I hoped that the sword
that struck me


01:14:11.527 --> 01:14:13.828
had not penetrated so deeply.


01:14:13.829 --> 01:14:18.401
I hoped to get back up
and fight by your side again.


01:14:20.903 --> 01:14:22.839
I hoped I would not die.


01:14:25.207 --> 01:14:27.475
Then I saw the blood,


01:14:27.476 --> 01:14:30.177
and I understood that I will
never fight again.


01:14:30.178 --> 01:14:34.015
But I still had hope,


01:14:34.016 --> 01:14:36.819
hope that you were alive.


01:14:39.821 --> 01:14:42.390
I hoped to see you
one more time.


01:14:42.391 --> 01:14:45.661
Our last journey together.


01:14:48.830 --> 01:14:51.532
And now I almost hope


01:14:51.533 --> 01:14:55.202
that we never reach
our destination.


01:14:55.203 --> 01:14:57.573
<i>The proof is incontestable,
my son.</i>


01:14:59.708 --> 01:15:02.510
They have seen her
more than once in the woods.


01:15:02.511 --> 01:15:07.415
We can no longer hide the truth.


01:15:07.416 --> 01:15:11.185
There are too many witnesses.


01:15:11.186 --> 01:15:14.422
And very soon,


01:15:14.423 --> 01:15:16.692
the Inquisition will come
to learn of these things.


01:15:20.028 --> 01:15:22.098
I will not do it.


01:15:24.933 --> 01:15:27.870
You ask too much of me, Father.


01:15:32.941 --> 01:15:35.977
I will go away with her.


01:15:35.978 --> 01:15:39.547
Somewhere they won't find us.


01:15:39.548 --> 01:15:41.482
These are the words of a fool.


01:15:41.483 --> 01:15:43.653
Would you risk your life
for a witch?


01:15:45.787 --> 01:15:47.790
Do not call her that.


01:15:51.727 --> 01:15:54.929
She is innocent, I'm sure.


01:15:54.930 --> 01:15:59.266
Well, if you believe
she is so innocent,


01:15:59.267 --> 01:16:03.971
then let the Church
carry out its investigation.


01:16:03.972 --> 01:16:07.910
I know the methods
of the tribunal.


01:16:09.478 --> 01:16:11.646
I would never live with myself.


01:16:11.647 --> 01:16:16.317
My son, I have known you
since you were a child.


01:16:16.318 --> 01:16:18.352
Listen to me.


01:16:18.353 --> 01:16:22.023
Think of the consequences should
you disappear with this woman.


01:16:22.024 --> 01:16:25.426
Times have changed.


01:16:25.427 --> 01:16:27.461
If you do not fear
for your own life,


01:16:27.462 --> 01:16:29.822
then think of the untold grief
that will befall your family.


01:16:33.335 --> 01:16:36.272
Help me, father.


01:16:41.610 --> 01:16:44.380
Be wise, my son.


01:16:45.947 --> 01:16:48.884
It is really very simple.


01:16:52.354 --> 01:16:54.989
Let the Inquisition
carry out the interrogation.


01:16:54.990 --> 01:16:58.225
In the meantime,


01:16:58.226 --> 01:17:02.530
you should return to the front.


01:17:02.531 --> 01:17:06.333
And you will see,


01:17:06.334 --> 01:17:10.239
on your return,
all will have been resolved.


01:17:11.807 --> 01:17:15.576
Mark my words.


01:17:15.577 --> 01:17:18.147
And may God go with you.


01:22:23.952 --> 01:22:25.721
You've travelled long.


01:22:31.159 --> 01:22:34.661
I am lost.


01:22:34.662 --> 01:22:36.565
This is the right direction.


01:22:42.404 --> 01:22:44.340
Why am I here?


01:22:48.977 --> 01:22:51.078
This is not the way home.


01:22:51.079 --> 01:22:53.682
And where is your home?


01:22:56.184 --> 01:22:59.186
East.


01:22:59.187 --> 01:23:03.390
What is this place?


01:23:03.391 --> 01:23:06.461
Somebody else's home, I believe.


01:23:09.697 --> 01:23:11.600
I don't understand.


01:23:13.868 --> 01:23:17.172
It's difficult to comprehend
time as it passes.


01:23:19.874 --> 01:23:22.242
You have travelled far.


01:23:22.243 --> 01:23:24.912
more than you can imagine.


01:23:24.913 --> 01:23:27.850
For days I haven't seen
the Morning Star.


01:23:30.552 --> 01:23:32.454
The nights are darker.


01:23:36.391 --> 01:23:40.928
Why are you here?


01:23:40.929 --> 01:23:43.032
I know you!


01:23:45.400 --> 01:23:48.470
Are you sure?


01:23:50.738 --> 01:23:52.372
No.


01:23:52.373 --> 01:23:54.408
Another place,


01:23:54.409 --> 01:23:57.946
another time.


01:23:59.047 --> 01:24:01.248
I want to go home.


01:24:01.249 --> 01:24:04.418
I want peace.


01:24:04.419 --> 01:24:06.321
Peace?


01:24:08.590 --> 01:24:10.993
Is peace what you deserve?


01:24:17.165 --> 01:24:19.101
I didn't do anything!


01:24:24.939 --> 01:24:27.009
Why are you doing this to me?


01:24:30.278 --> 01:24:32.181
I only did what had to be done.


01:26:02.537 --> 01:26:05.205
Why?


01:26:05.206 --> 01:26:08.909
Do you still not remember?


01:26:08.910 --> 01:26:10.846
Remember what?


01:26:13.581 --> 01:26:15.517
Me.

